{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/src/node.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T12:16:47.310770Z","id":"a0937fc2020a2f554080a1b7345cae32c4ac91accde3c4d02c6dbbae29446a0a","body":{"detail":"Failure: in a five-voter Cluster (ids 1..5, fresh state), node 1 wins pre-votes from 3 and 4, campaigns in term 1, and only node 3 receives its Vote request. Node 3 grants, and that Voted{term:1,granted:true} is delayed. Node 2 then pre-votes and campaigns in term 1 with nodes 4 and 5 and becomes Leader of term 1 (2,4,5 voted for it). Node 1 times out while still Candidate. tick() (node.rs:360-375) sets prevoting=Some(2), clears `votes` to {1}, and leaves `role == Role::Candidate` and hard.term == 1. Node 4 has not yet heard an Append from node 2 and grants PreVoted{campaign:2}, so node 1's votes become {1,4}. The delayed Voted{term:1,granted:true} from node 3 then arrives. step() treats it as current-term (node.rs:449 does not reject it), and the Voted arm (node.rs:487-493) only checks `self.role == Role::Candidate`. It sets votes[3]=true, election_quorum() sees {1,3,4}, and become_leader() runs in term 1. Result: nodes 1 and 2 are both Leader in term 1. Each appends its own barrier (index 1, term 1), so one LogId names entries from two leaders, which violates Election Safety and Log Matching (Raft paper Figure 3, https://raft.github.io/raft.pdf). I reproduced this with the public Cluster API (tick/step/ready/next_message) in a throwaway binary outside the repository: final output `A role Leader term 1; B role Leader term 1`. The root cause is that pre-vote grants (which are for term 2 and are not durable votes) and real term-1 votes are counted in the same `votes` array. The Voted handler cannot tell which kind it is counting while `prevoting.is_some()`. The fixed `Node` (hooks None) is not affected because its tick() calls campaign() directly.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":360},"end":{"line":375},"content_hash":"eb68a0b2536c8898ae3945a2fce584343851b3c81eb5a08f1e93a13c364860f5"},"suggested_fix":"When starting a pre-vote in tick(), step down to a non-candidate state (set `self.role = Role::Follower`, as the Raft thesis pre-candidate does), or guard the Voted arm with `self.prevoting.is_none()`. Better still, track pre-vote grants in a separate array from real votes. Add a regression test with the five-node schedule above that asserts at most one leader per term.","summary":"A Candidate that starts a pre-vote keeps role Candidate and shares `votes` with the probe, so a late same-term Voted grant plus pre-vote grants elect it leader of the old term, which breaks election safety","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/src/node.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T12:25:07.514013Z","id":"2773c2689bad46afd14ed5a54e54f7a71f2e4b5e9458ef436bfe7cb33ac237d3","body":{"detail":"At HEAD jarl/src/node.rs: tick() with hooks (360-375) sets prevoting=Some(term+1), resets votes to {self}, and does not change role or hard.term. step() records PreVoted grants into the same votes array (441-442). A same-term Voted passes the stale check (449), and the Voted arm (487-493) checks only role == Candidate before setting votes[peer] and calling become_leader(). PreVote grant (413-418) needs only term > hard.term, role != Leader, and leader_age >= election_ticks; leader_age starts at u64::MAX (150), so a follower that has voted but not yet heard an Append still grants. Reproduced against jarl at the HEAD source (git diff HEAD -- jarl/src is empty) with a standalone binary that uses Cluster<u8,u8,5,16> through tick/step/ready/next_message only, ids 1..5, Settings{heartbeat 2, election 10}. Trace: 1->3,1->4 PreVote(1) granted; node1 Candidate term 1; 1->3 Vote(1), reply 3->1 Voted(1,true) held; node 2 pre-votes and votes with 4,5 and becomes Leader term 1; node1 ticks to timeout and stays Candidate term 1; 1->4 PreVote(2) -> 4->1 PreVoted(t1,c2,true); held 3->1 Voted(1,true) delivered. Final output: `A role Leader term 1; B role Leader term 1`. Two leaders in one term violate Election Safety, so blocker is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"a0937fc2020a2f554080a1b7345cae32c4ac91accde3c4d02c6dbbae29446a0a","summary":"confirmed: a Candidate that starts a pre-vote keeps role Candidate, and a late term-1 Voted grant plus pre-vote grants elect a second term-1 leader","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
